TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"attempt":2,"blocked":true,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/8","kind":"diagnosis","posted":true,"proposal":{"acceptanceCriteria":[{"argv":["bash","-euc","bash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'results/receipts/proxy.json' scripts/run-proxy.sh"],"description":"Both scripts are syntax-clean and reference the receipt path.","id":"proxy-scripts-clean"},{"argv":["bash","-euc","git ls-files --error-unmatch scripts/make-proxy.sh scripts/run-proxy.sh >/dev/null && test -z \"$(git status --porcelain)\""],"description":"Both scripts are tracked at HEAD and the worktree is clean, which is the condition attempts 1 and 2 failed.","id":"proxy-scripts-committed"},{"argv":["bash","-euc","grep -q 'VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1' scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'limit-mm-per-prompt' scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -qi 'enforce.eager\\|enforce_eager' scripts/run-proxy.sh"],"description":"run-proxy.sh encodes the established serve doctrine so cp-proxy and the later TP=2 serve reproduce it: PLE mmap on, eager execution, and text-only multimodal limits.","id":"proxy-serve-flags-recorded"},{"argv":["bash","-euc","git diff --name-only 71f2beba0ecd7358eda99e574e078d081f55bbfa..HEAD | grep -vE '^(scripts/make-proxy\\.sh|scripts/run-proxy\\.sh|tests/|results/receipts/proxy\\.json$)' | { ! grep -q .; }"],"description":"Every path touched by the task commits stays inside the amended boundary, including the receipt.","id":"proxy-no-out-of-domain-paths"}],"dependencies":[],"goal":"Re-issue the proxy-tooling work with results/receipts/proxy.json added to the write boundary and with a commit-first ordering that decouples authoring the scripts from exercising them on the GPU. Deliverable 1 (must land as a commit before any container or GPU work begins): scripts/make-proxy.sh and scripts/run-proxy.sh written in the style of scripts/run-smoke.sh (bash shebang, set -euo pipefail, REPO_ROOT derived from dirname, IMAGE=\"${FN_IMAGE:-flashnext:dev}\", podman run with --device /dev/kfd --device /dev/dri --security-opt seccomp=unconfined --ipc=host and -v \"$REPO_ROOT/results:/results\", heredoc'd python payload), per specs/flashnext/spec.md#r4 and the cited evidence notes. make-proxy.sh runs inside the container and synthesizes a tiny checkpoint under /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy — same architecture identifier as the workload, a handful of layers, 8 experts in block-FP8 with weight_block_size 128 by 128, and a small lookup table using the shard tensor name the mmap path expects — reusing the fork's own tests/models/ scaffolding inside the fork checkout rather than inventing a generator, and it must not assume /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy already exists because it does not. run-proxy.sh serves that checkpoint single-node with VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1, eager execution, gpu_memory_utilization 0.6, and --limit-mm-per-prompt '{\"image\":0,\"video\":0}' (text-only mode, which is what avoids the 274877906944-byte vision-encoder profiling allocation), requests one greedy completion, asserts finite logits through the API, shuts down cleanly, writes results/receipts/proxy.json, and records the text-only flag choice in the receipt data so cp-proxy and the later TP=2 serve reproduce it. Deliverable 2 (separate commit, after the first has landed): the receipt produced by an actual run, now inside the boundary. The worker must finish every attempt with a clean `git status --porcelain`.","kind":"amendment-task","paths":["scripts/make-proxy.sh","scripts/run-proxy.sh","tests","results/receipts/proxy.json"]},"redacted":true,"retry":null,"taskId":"proxy-tooling","verdict":"blocked"}
